A||||4||Alex2004||Recalibrating 6 cyl tach to 4||||1||
Z||000000||Alex2004||10-20-2001||12:50 PM||||Yesterday i bought a backlit cluster (120 speedo, fuel & temp, and tach) from an 86 GT but i didn't buy the aux. yet.  Anyways, i'm wondering how to recalibrate the tach.  I have an 84 se and right now w/ the V6 tach it's reading about 1K -1.5K off (i think).  Also, one more question.  The Temp light stay's on.  On My old one it never came on but i know the bulb is good, but on this cluster it's staying on, the car wasn't hot though. What's causeing that?  Lemme know!  Thanks<P>Alex...<p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 10-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-20-2001||11:10 PM||||It is very simple to get your V6 tach to work with a 4 cyl.  Take the circuit board of the back of your 4 cyl tach, and then put it on the V6 tach.  Done.<P>As for the temp warning light, there could be a variety of reasons that it is on.  Short to groud @ sensor connector, bad sensor, short somewhere along the wiring in the engine compartment, interior or even right at the gauge cluster.  Try to trace as much of its wiring as you can.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LS1swap||10-21-2001||09:22 PM||||this might help <A HREF="http://www.fieros.de/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieros.de/</A>  go to articles and trouble shooting then tach rev. eng.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gerald||10-22-2001||10:04 PM||||Itried swaping the v6 tack to the 4 cyl cirkit borad and it still didnt work right. It reads about 1200rpm slow. what do i do?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex2004||10-22-2001||10:20 PM||||Well i figured out the prob w/ my temp light, i need to switch the plastic deals w/ turn, bright, deck ajar door ajar..LoL. i had the door open and with the temp light on the 86 cluster is where the temp light is, on the 84, door ajar.  Thanks about the circut board. i'll do that tomorrow!<P>Alex...||||reg||1
